## Grounding memory: current Athanor/Ahmes discovery

The first all-project vector pass used the CV descriptors:

```text
digital images, photography, image synthesis, authorship, semiotics,
generative art, data visualisation, ontology, AI imagery, digitisation,
human–AI collaboration, fashion communication
```

The retained evidence and discovery routes are recorded in
`forge/IMAGE-ONTOLOGY-GROUNDING-RECEIPT.md`. The receipt is a search memory,
not a bibliography shortcut: vector proximity is discovery only; every claim
must still pass complete-node reading and the Ahmes citation resolver.

Strong verified matches currently available:

- Shinkle, Eugénie, ed. 2008. *Fashion as Photograph: Viewing and Reviewing
  Images of Fashion*. `(Shinkle 2008, 50)`. Use for photographic truth,
  construction, and fashion-image practice.
- Bendel, Oliver. 2025. “Image Synthesis from an Ethical Perspective.” *AI &
  Society*. `(Bendel 2025, 1)`. DOI: `10.1007/s00146-023-01780-4`. Use for
  distinguishing image synthesis from photographic capture and for ethical
  questions around generated images.

Strong conceptual routes for later retrieval:

- generative AI and image synthesis;
- ethical issues in generated images;
- the transformation of the image through digitisation;
- image semiotics in fashion communication;
- digital authorship and human–AI collaboration;
- ontology as a formal vocabulary for classification;
- data and computational image production.

Fontcuberta remains a named target with a direct `[BIBLIO-GAP]` until a
canonical Ahmes node is ingested and resolved. Do not manufacture a quotation.
